  "body": "My `<head>` contains `<meta http-equiv=\"x-dns-prefetch-control\" content=\"on\">` but the validator marks it as an error with:\r\n\r\n> Bad value `x-dns-prefetch-control` for attribute `http-equiv` on element `meta`.\r\n\r\nIt appears to be a legal value.\r\n\r\n* https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X-DNS-Prefetch-Control\r\n\r\nAlthough I note it isn't enumerated as a pragma directive:\r\n\r\n* https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#pragma-directives\r\n\r\nDespite being supported in \r\n\r\n* Chrome https://www.chromium.org/developers/design-documents/dns-prefetching#TOC-DNS-Prefetch-Control\r\n* Firefox https://bitsup.blogspot.com/2008/11/dns-prefetching-for-firefox.html\r\n\r\nAre you happy for me to add this as a legitimate value in the spec?",
